### What would you like to be added?

In Kubernetes, the ClusterFirst policy is the default policy for deploying pods. However, it seems that the /etc/resolv.conf file for pods does not have any global options for configuring DNS.

Our pods not only need to access cluster services but also need to access cluster external services. This involves cluster and external domain name resolution. If the DNSConfig  is not properly configured, the default search configuration  will result in a lot of unnecessary DNS queries. We use fully qualified domain names (FQDNs) to request services. In this case, the search parameter is unnecessary. We expect to be able to configure the search parameter globally and the number of dots to be written to the pod's /etc/resolv.conf file.

about source code:  https://github.com/kubernetes/kubernetes/blob/master/pkg/kubelet/network/dns/dns.go#L385

```go
	case podDNSCluster:
		if len(c.clusterDNS) != 0 {
			// For a pod with DNSClusterFirst policy, the cluster DNS server is
			// the only nameserver configured for the pod. The cluster DNS server
			// itself will forward queries to other nameservers that is configured
			// to use, in case the cluster DNS server cannot resolve the DNS query
			// itself.
			dnsConfig.Servers = []string{}
			for _, ip := range c.clusterDNS {
				dnsConfig.Servers = append(dnsConfig.Servers, ip.String())
			}
			dnsConfig.Searches = c.generateSearchesForDNSClusterFirst(dnsConfig.Searches, pod)
			dnsConfig.Options = defaultDNSOptions
			break
		}
		// clusterDNS is not known. Pod with ClusterDNSFirst Policy cannot be created.
		nodeErrorMsg := fmt.Sprintf("kubelet does not have ClusterDNS IP configured and cannot create Pod using %q policy. Falling back to %q policy.", v1.DNSClusterFirst, v1.DNSDefault)
		c.recorder.Eventf(c.nodeRef, v1.EventTypeWarning, "MissingClusterDNS", nodeErrorMsg)
		c.recorder.Eventf(pod, v1.EventTypeWarning, "MissingClusterDNS", "pod: %q. %s", format.Pod(pod), nodeErrorMsg)
		// Fallback to DNSDefault.
		fallthrough
```

### Why is this needed?

There are no global configuration options, and it's inconvenient to configure one by one in pods through DNSConfig.

